From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:32:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The land's trees' sun shadows: Eterna's and Celestic's firs,
 the Great Marsh's stumps (SDK_PORT_3DS)

Every tree texture of the maps' land models was looked for; three more
are trees to the port (their layers lit by the sun, their shadows laid):
g1_treea and g1_treeb, Eterna City's and Celestic Town's small firs, and
numa_ki, the Great Marsh's stumps. Left as they are: the Battle
Frontier's (bf_tree02 is its palm grove's sheet of leaves, with black
specks as trees; its cone tree has a shadow painted beside it), the
Distortion World's (no sun there) and those of rooms.
---
 src/overlay005/land_data.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 6e813f14..03e251da 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -78,6 +78,15 @@ static const char *const sPortTreeTextures[] = {
     "tree01", "tree2_01", "tree04_2", "tree3_01", "tree3_02",
     "conttree_b", "conttree_t", "conttree2_b", "conttree2_t", "conttree3_2",
     "treeeff01",
+    // (2026-11-12, every tree texture of the maps looked for, "trees that
+    // should cast shadows must do so consistently": Eterna City's and
+    // Celestic Town's small firs, and the Great Marsh's stumps. Not the
+    // Battle Frontier's (bf_tree02 is its palm grove's one sheet of
+    // leaves: black specks in it as trees; its cone tree has a shadow
+    // painted beside it, and bf_tree01 and bf_tree03 showed none of the
+    // sun's), not the Distortion World's (tree_sbt01: no sun there), not
+    // those of rooms (a gym's, the League's).)
+    "g1_treea", "g1_treeb", "numa_ki",
 };
 
 // A land model's trees, kept by its material block's address until that
